  "description": "Unresolved emotions never fade away. Love turns into a wound, and that wound becomes a song, reappearing before him after seven years. Bae Yeon-U, an Olympic silver medalist and professional tennis player. Song Hyeon-Seung, known as “Silver,” the vocalist of the top band NIGHTSOUL. Two boys who first met in an abandoned warehouse and became each other’s entire world. But Yeon-U, hounded by poverty, debt, and violence, leaves Korea, leaving behind his family, love, and everything else in pursuit of success. Seven years later. Both have reached the pinnacle of their respective worlds. Yeon-U remains in every one of Hyeon-Seung’s songs, and Hyeon-Seung lives on behind every one of Yeon-U’s victories.\n\n *“You’ve always been my biggest regret in life.”*\n\nA first love they thought was over, time, which had stood still, begins to flow once more.\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
